# Mobile floor aesthetic

When changing UI in these folders, follow `.cursor/skills/mobile-floor-aesthetic/SKILL.md`.

- Boards on parchment: `radius.xl`, `borderStrong`, `surface`, `orderBoardShadow`, 3px brand rail at reading-start, header band, inset meta.
- Press: `AnimatedPressable` + `haptics`. Cards `0.985`, buttons `0.97`.
- Pop-ups: shared `BottomSheet` with the same boards/chips — not flat iOS forms.
- Touch bars: copy `PurchasingTabBar` / `ReportsTabBar` / `ProductionHubJump` / `UsersSegmentRail` (pill bubble), floor triggers, `DealerSummaryRail`, or `OrdersRfqInboxChips` (Factory review 3+2 cells). No Material chips.
- Arabic: `medium` titles, no uppercase. Money/codes `dir="ltr"`.
- No white cards, traffic colors, FABs, or new hex outside existing wood-pill arrays.

Canonical copies: `DealerBoard`, `InvoiceBoardCard`, `PurchaseOrderBoardCard`, `UserBoardCard`, `ReportsTabBar`, `ProductionOrderCard`, `ProductionIdentityBoard`, `ProductionMaterialUsageBoard`, `InventoryBoardCard`, `InventoryIdentityBoard`, `InventoryMaterialRow`, `OrdersRfqInboxChips`, `OrdersFilterButton`, `OrdersFilterSheet`, `RequestIdentityBoard`, `RfqStageRail`.

Production, inventory, and orders may use a different stack (hub jump / lifecycle+section chrome / All orders vs Factory review) but the board recipe stays the same. No `DeskCard` / `SurfaceCard` / `colors.info` on those floors.
